  },
  {
   "id": "04cf16dd826e",
   "unit_id": "04cf16dd826ecc9c57606da4e35c906816b88f94a79921224d230c2f05840ca7",
   "revision_key": "71b220a099931cc5c164501d5d69341f5a1f00fcb205f6170aac29f4c92cfcb8",
   "translation_file": "mod-tome.lua",
   "translation_line": 5076,
   "section": "mod-tome/data/chats/gates-of-morning-main.lua",
   "source_tag": "_t",
   "args_order": null,
   "source": "The people you saw are likely the volunteers of Zemekkys' early experiments regarding the farportals.\nHe is a mage who resides here in the Sunwall, eccentric but skilled, who believes that creation of a new farportal to Maj'Eyal is possible.\nAside from a few early attempts with questionable results, he hasn't had much luck. Still, it's gladdening to hear that the volunteers for his experiments live, regardless of their location. We are all still under the same Sun, after all.\n\nActually... maybe it would benefit you if you meet Zemekkys. He would surely be intrigued by that Orb of Many Ways you possess. He lives in a small house just to the north.",
   "target": "你看到的那些人很可能是参加泽梅基斯早期远行传送门实验的志愿者。\n他是居住在太阳堡垒的一个法师，脾气古怪但是很有能力，他坚信可以建造一座通往马基·埃亚尔的新远行传送门。\n除了早期几次结果存疑的尝试外，他一直没什么进展。不过，听说参加他实验的志愿者还活着，还是让人高兴，不管他们身在何方。毕竟我们都生活在同一片阳光下。\n\n事实上……也许去见见泽梅基斯对你有好处。他一定会对你手上的多元水晶球感兴趣。他就住在北边的小屋里。",
   "source_file": "game/modules/tome/data/chats/gates-of-morning-main.lua @ 624a67329fe2 (pinned core)",
   "source_lines": [
    61
   ],
   "previously_reviewed": {
    "A": false,
    "B": false
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "2120b32921bd",
   "unit_id": "2120b32921bd290926fadec03a69299a95ec84aaf14e8a8ed65508efa73d2914",
   "revision_key": "ea460b946d176ff31f9778ac18eeb073d3f7a05fe467c4cbfc70adc811060237",
   "translation_file": "mod-tome.lua",
   "translation_line": 5085,
   "section": "mod-tome/data/chats/gates-of-morning-main.lua",
   "source_tag": "_t",
   "args_order": null,
   "source": "Maybe I'll visit him. Thank you.",
   "target": "也许我会见见他，谢谢。",
   "source_file": "game/modules/tome/data/chats/gates-of-morning-main.lua @ 624a67329fe2 (pinned core)",
   "source_lines": [
    67
   ],
   "previously_reviewed": {
